<div class="wrap">
<header class="mast">
  <div class="kicker">
    <span>Implementation spec</span><span class="sep">/</span>
    <span>entireio&#47;cli</span><span class="sep">/</span>
    <span>Stage&nbsp;C</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Condense at Stop, link at commit</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">When the committer was human, the commit was a curation event and anchoring capture to it was right. The commit is now a tool call inside a turn — still the right linkage anchor, no longer the right capture trigger.</p>
  <div class="meta">
    <span><b>Status</b> spec, not implemented</span>
    <span><b>Companion</b> overview.md §6, §8</span>
    <span><b>Ships</b> fork A</span>
    <span><b>Date</b> 2026-08-31</span>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="scope">
  <h2>Read this first</h2>
  <p>This stage ships <strong>fork A — start-only transcript offsets</strong>. Token attribution is <strong>not</strong> fixed here, and saying otherwise was the contradiction that six review passes surfaced: bounded <code>[start, end)</code> windows require a metadata field that does not exist, and adding one destroys the per-developer trialability the whole rollout depends on.</p>
  <p>Every code claim below cites its <em>enclosing function</em>, not just a line number. Three errors in the research doc came from reading grep hits without their surrounding context; all 24 citations here were resolved against the tree before publishing.</p>
</div>

<div class="cols">
  <nav class="rail" aria-label="Sections">
