  <main>
    <section id="s1">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">01</span><h2 class="st">What this changes</h2></div>
      <p>For <strong>ACTIVE sessions only</strong>, <code>PostCommit</code> stops condensing and instead completes a durable <em>commit-link record</em>; <code>HandleTurnEnd</code> performs one condensation pass that materializes every record from the turn. IDLE and ENDED commits are untouched — for them the turn is already over, so condense-at-commit <em>is</em> condense-at-turn-end.</p>
      <p>Today's ACTIVE path writes a provisional checkpoint per commit via <code>CondenseSession</code> <span class="cite">manual_commit_condensation.go:514</span>, which falls back to the live transcript when the shadow branch is absent, then rewrites all of them at turn end through <code>finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints</code>. This stage removes the first draft.</p>

      <div class="panel">
        <h3>What it delivers</h3>
        <ol class="inv">
          <li><strong>A dangling trailer becomes repairable.</strong> The intent is persisted outside the commit message, so a crash between commit and Stop is recoverable rather than permanent and undetectable.</li>
          <li><strong>One condensation per turn</strong> instead of N provisional writes plus N rewrites — including one compact-transcript regeneration rather than one per commit.</li>
          <li><strong>Real per-commit diff files</strong> in metadata, replacing today's <code>FilesTouched ∩ committed</code> approximation. Same field, better content; not a format change.</li>
          <li><strong>Turn intents survive process death,</strong> replacing <code>TurnCheckpointIDs</code> <span class="cite">session/state.go:207</span>, which <code>InitializeSession</code> clears at the next TurnStart.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="panel warnpanel">
        <h3>Non-goals</h3>
        <p><strong>Token attribution is unchanged.</strong> Fixing it needs bounded <code>[start, end)</code> windows, which needs a field that does not exist: <code>writeSession</code> persists <code>CheckpointTranscriptStart</code> only <span class="cite">checkpoint/persistent.go:736</span>, and <code>scopeTranscriptForCheckpoint</code> <span class="cite">explain.go:1865</span> slices from that offset to the transcript end. An older reader handed a bounded-window checkpoint would render start→end-of-transcript, over-reporting later commits' content. The token fix is a <strong>separate, format-versioned change</strong>; the finalize token bug stays a standalone bugfix valid under both models.</p>
        <p><strong>Turn-tail semantics dissolve here.</strong> Under start-only windows every checkpoint's window runs to the transcript end, so the tail is already shared exactly as today. The question only becomes real under the later bounded-window change.</p>
        <p><strong>Also out:</strong> linked-worktree capture (§2 — prerequisite, not part of this stage) and hook <em>delivery</em> misses such as <code>--no-verify</code>, <code>core.hooksPath=''</code> and non-hook commit tools, which belong to the reconciliation track.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="s2">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">02</span><h2 class="st">Prerequisite: event-scoped worktree resolution</h2></div>
      <p><strong>This stage must not ship before it.</strong> In the cwd-stays-in-main worktree case Stop has no content, so a link record would materialize against nothing — turning today's <em>mislabeled</em> checkpoint into a <em>dangling</em> one.</p>
      <p>The fix is <strong>not parser work</strong>. <code>SaveStep</code> <span class="cite">manual_commit_git.go:27</span> and <code>PostCommit</code> <span class="cite">manual_commit_hooks.go:930</span> both open the repo via <code>OpenRepository(ctx)</code> → <code>gitrepo.OpenCurrent(ctx)</code> <span class="cite">strategy/common.go:1361</span>, which takes no worktree argument and resolves from the <em>process</em> cwd. Populating <code>agent.Event.CWD</code> without threading it into that open changes nothing at Stop.</p>
      <p><code>Event.CWD</code> is also ToolUse-scoped by contract — <span class="cite">agent/event.go:158</span> reads <em>“Set on ToolUse so cwd-relative payload paths can be resolved before repo-root normalization”</em> — with a single consumer in <code>normalizeToolUsePaths</code> <span class="cite">lifecycle.go:373</span>. Using it at turn end widens that contract.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s3">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">03</span><h2 class="st">The commit-link journal</h2></div>
      <p><strong>Name.</strong> “Sidecar” is unavailable: <code>SidecarImageProvider</code> <span class="cite">agent/capabilities.go:100</span> already owns it for image assets. Use <strong>journal</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Location.</strong> <code>&lt;git-common-dir&gt;/entire-commit-links/&lt;checkpoint-id&gt;.json</code> — one file per checkpoint ID, in the common dir so worktrees share it, matching <code>.git/entire-sessions/&lt;id&gt;.json</code>.</p>
      <p><strong>Not</strong> new fields on <code>session.State</code>: an older CLI in a sibling worktree round-trips that file and drops unknown fields. That is also why this cannot extend <code>CondensationAttempt</code> <span class="cite">session/state.go:104</span> in place — that type lives <em>inside</em> the state JSON and holds exactly one attempt per session, where a turn needs N.</p>
      <p><strong>One file per ID, not one shared journal,</strong> so concurrent commits in different worktrees never contend. Writes are atomic rename; a per-file lock follows the precedent of <code>capturedSyncRemotesFileName</code> <span class="cite">strategy/checkpoint_sync_capture.go:22</span>.</p>
<pre><code>{
  <span class="key">"checkpoint_id"</span>: "a1b2c3d4e5f6",
  <span class="key">"phase"</span>: "intent" | "linked",
  <span class="key">"created_at"</span>: "2026-08-31T12:00:00Z",
  <span class="key">"worktree_id"</span>: "&lt;worktree hash&gt;",     <span class="cmt">// whose commit this is</span>
  <span class="key">"sessions"</span>: [                          <span class="cmt">// PLURAL — see below</span>
    { "session_id": "…", "transcript_offset": 412 }
  ],
  <span class="key">"commit_sha"</span>: "…",                     <span class="cmt">// phase 2 only</span>
  <span class="key">"committed_files"</span>: ["a.go", "b.go"]    <span class="cmt">// phase 2 only, real diff</span>
}</code></pre>
      <p class="cap">One checkpoint ID already spans every session a commit condenses: <code>checkpointIDForSessions</code> takes <code>[]*SessionState</code> and reuses whichever session already holds a <code>PendingCondensationID</code> <span class="cite">manual_commit_hooks.go:2352</span>. Each session offsets into its own transcript, so the offset is per-session, not per-record.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s4">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">04</span><h2 class="st">Phase 1 — prepare-commit-msg</h2></div>
      <p><code>PrepareCommitMsg</code> <span class="cite">manual_commit_hooks.go:358</span> already reserves a stable ID and stamps the trailer. It additionally writes a <code>phase: "intent"</code> journal file.</p>
      <p><strong>Ordering.</strong> The journal write must be durable <em>before</em> the trailer is stamped, or a crash between the two yields exactly the dangling trailer this stage exists to remove. Use <code>MutateSessionStateOnSaved</code> <span class="cite">strategy/session_state.go:599</span>, which exists precisely for a side effect that must follow a durable write — its doc notes that <code>MutateSessionState</code> returning nil “is not proof that anything was written.”</p>

      <figure class="tl">
        <div class="tl-scroll">
          <div class="tl-grid">
            <div class="tl-axis"></div>
            <div class="tl-stop">
              <p class="tl-when">prepare-commit-msg</p>
              <p class="tl-what">ID reserved, trailer stamped, intent written. <strong>No SHA exists yet.</strong></p>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-stop plain">
              <p class="tl-when">git writes commit</p>
              <p class="tl-what">The object now exists. No hook runs here.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-stop">
              <p class="tl-when">post-commit</p>
              <p class="tl-what">SHA and real diff known. Record completed; condensation skipped.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="tl-stop">
              <p class="tl-when">Stop &middot; HandleTurnEnd</p>
              <p class="tl-what">One condensation pass drains every record from the turn.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-bars">
            <div class="bar w" style="grid-column:1/3">dangling-trailer window today — permanent if the process dies</div>
            <div class="bar" style="grid-column:3/5">pending window under this stage — recoverable, §8</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption>The SHA is unavailable at the moment the ID is minted. That gap is why the record is two-phase, and it is the same gap today's dangling trailer falls into.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>Phase-1 records are <strong>provisional</strong>. prepare-commit-msg also runs for commits that are then aborted, and removing the trailer is a <em>supported</em> opt-out: the hook documents it as “useful for manual commits,” and <code>PostCommit</code> no-ops when the trailer is absent, updating only <code>BaseCommit</code> via <code>postCommitUpdateBaseCommitOnly</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s5">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">05</span><h2 class="st">Phase 2 — post-commit</h2></div>
      <p>Inside the per-session loop <span class="cite">manual_commit_hooks.go:1055</span>, for sessions where <code>state.Phase.IsActive()</code>:</p>
      <ol class="body">
        <li>Complete the journal file → <code>phase: "linked"</code>, adding <code>commit_sha</code> (HEAD) and <code>committed_files</code> (the actual commit diff).</li>
        <li><strong>Skip condensation.</strong> Do not call <code>CondenseSession</code>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Non-ACTIVE sessions keep today's behaviour exactly, including the <code>sessionHasNewContent</code> check and the <code>filesTouchedBefore</code> copy.</p>
      <p><strong>Collision is a detector, not a hazard.</strong> Because <code>checkpointIDForSessions</code> reuses a session's <code>PendingCondensationID</code>, two concurrent guest-linked commits can in principle claim one ID. If phase 2 finds a file already <code>linked</code> with a <em>different</em> <code>commit_sha</code>, that is a breach of invariant 2: log loudly and refuse rather than overwrite. This is adjacent to the un-CAS'd <code>SetReference</code> in <code>writeSession</code> and does not fix it.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s6">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">06</span><h2 class="st">Stop — materialization</h2></div>
      <p><code>HandleTurnEnd</code> <span class="cite">manual_commit_hooks.go:2900</span> enumerates <code>entire-commit-links/</code> for this worktree and, for each <code>linked</code> record, calls <code>CondenseSession</code> once — the <strong>create</strong> path, since today's <code>finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints</code> is an <em>update</em> and cannot be the sole writer. <code>CondenseSession</code> already accepts <code>committedFiles map[string]struct{}</code>, which the record's <code>committed_files</code> feeds directly.</p>
      <p>All of a turn's checkpoints receive identical transcript bytes, so they dedup to one git blob — the same end state finalize produces today.</p>
      <p>Delete each record only after its checkpoint write succeeds. A record surviving a failed write <em>is</em> the retry signal.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s7">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">07</span><h2 class="st">The drain predicate</h2></div>
      <p style="font-family:var(--display); font-size:1.12rem; font-style:italic; color:var(--ink); border-left:2px solid var(--accent); padding-left:16px; margin:0 0 16px">An intent materializes only if some commit actually carries its ID.</p>
      <p>Positive, never “the record is old.” The two obligations pull against each other and both must hold.</p>
      <div class="tscroll">
        <table>
          <caption>Drain decisions</caption>
          <thead><tr><th>Record state</th><th>Commit carrying the ID?</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>linked</code></td><td>yes — <code>commit_sha</code> recorded</td><td class="act keep">materialize</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>intent</code></td><td>yes — found by search</td><td class="act keep">complete, then materialize</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>intent</code></td><td>no</td><td class="act discard">discard — aborted commit, or trailer removed</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>linked</code></td><td>SHA no longer reachable</td><td class="act discard">discard — rebased or amended away</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Lookup precedent: <code>getAssociatedCommits</code> <span class="cite">explain.go:1787</span> already searches commits for <code>Entire-Checkpoint</code> trailer matches, bounded to the current branch by default with <code>searchAll</code> for a full DAG walk. The sweep uses the bounded form; an intent whose commit is not found within the bound is <strong>left in place and retried, not discarded</strong> — discarding needs positive evidence of absence, not a failed search.</p>
      <p>Anything weaker resurrects checkpoints someone deliberately declined.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s8">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">08</span><h2 class="st">Recovery sweep</h2></div>
      <p>The sweep is <strong>load-bearing, not a nicety</strong>, because push is only a best-effort barrier (§9). It ships <em>with</em> the flag, not after it.</p>
      <p>It runs where <code>finalizeExitedSessions</code> <span class="cite">session_finalize.go:55</span> already runs — <span class="cite">session_sweep.go:100</span> unbudgeted, <span class="cite">status.go:484</span>, and <span class="cite">doctor.go:178</span> with <code>interactiveSweepCondenseBudget</code> — plus the next TurnStart. Reuse that budget convention so a backlog drains across invocations instead of stalling one.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s9">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">09</span><h2 class="st">Push barrier</h2></div>
      <p>Pre-push materializes pending records before checkpoint refs leave the machine — redaction has to run there anyway. It is <strong>best-effort</strong>: the only production caller of <code>PrePushFromGitHook</code> is the pre-push cobra command <span class="cite">hooks_git_cmd.go:324</span>, so <code>push --no-verify</code> walks straight past it. That is precisely why §8 is load-bearing.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s10">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">10</span><h2 class="st">Read side</h2></div>
      <p><code>explain</code> and <code>checkpoint list</code> may be handed an ID whose checkpoint does not exist yet. Report it as <strong>pending</strong>, with the commit SHA. Do not synthesize checkpoint content from the live transcript in this stage — that adds a second read path for a window measured in minutes.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s11">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">11</span><h2 class="st">The flag</h2></div>
      <p><code>strategy_options.condense_at_turn_end</code>, default <strong>off</strong>. <code>StrategyOptions</code> is <code>map[string]any</code> <span class="cite">settings/settings.go:95</span>, so no schema change is needed. Honored from <code>settings.local.json</code> for per-developer trial.</p>
      <p>Rollback is flag off: the sweep drains records written under either timing, and under fork A no reader can tell which timing produced a checkpoint.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="s12">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">12</span><h2 class="st">Invariants</h2></div>
      <ol class="inv">
        <li>Every commit gets its own unique checkpoint ID.</li>
        <li>A checkpoint is never attached to two commits — §5 detects a breach.</li>
        <li>The working branch is never touched.</li>
        <li>The privacy gradient is unchanged: local until push, configured redaction — regex-only by default, OPF's 9th layer where enabled — before anything leaves the machine.</li>
        <li>No checkpoint exists for a commit that does not carry its ID (§7).</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="s13">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">13</span><h2 class="st">Tests</h2></div>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li>Mid-turn commit + Stop → exactly one checkpoint, correct SHA and diff files.</li>
        <li>Two mid-turn commits + Stop → two checkpoints, one shared transcript blob.</li>
        <li class="star"><strong>Trailer removed after prepare → no checkpoint, record discarded.</strong> The opt-out regression test; this is the one the drain rule exists for.</li>
        <li>Aborted commit (empty message) → record discarded.</li>
        <li>Killed between commit and Stop → next TurnStart or <code>status</code> materializes it.</li>
        <li>IDLE commit → byte-identical behaviour to flag-off.</li>
        <li>Flag off → no journal files written at all.</li>
        <li>Concurrent guest-linked commits sharing an ID → breach logged, no overwrite.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="s14">
      <div class="sechead"><span class="num">14</span><h2 class="st">Deliberately open</h2></div>
      <ol class="inv">
        <li><strong>Bounded windows and token apportionment.</strong> A separate format-versioned change needing its own compatibility story — per-source <em>and</em> per-session, since hook-sourced counts carry no offset and <code>SubagentTokens</code> is replace-not-add inside <code>accumulateTokenUsage</code>.</li>
        <li>Whether <code>getAssociatedCommits</code>' default branch bound is wide enough for the sweep's discard decision, or whether discard should require <code>searchAll</code>.</li>
        <li>Interaction with the un-CAS'd v1 ref advance in <code>writeSession</code> — one condensation per turn narrows the concurrent-condenser window but does not close it.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <span>Source of truth: <code>stage-c-spec.md</code></span>
      <span>24 citations, all resolved against the tree</span>
    </footer>
  </main>
